Subject: [PATCH] Add policy comparison pipeline: sampler, metrics, plots,
 SLURM jobs

- sample_policies_mc.py: unified MC sampler for all acquisition policies
  (A0 random, A1 max_variance, A2 max_entropy, A5 growing, A6 pop_order,
  MSE oracle) using U3 full conditional re-sampling
- compute_population_order.py: greedy A6 population-optimised order from
  train/val ensemble variance (label-free, one fixed sequence for all patients)
- compute_metrics_policies.py: RMSE, MAE, MD-MAE, sLV-MAE per-k, per-severity
  stratum (normal/early/moderate/advanced/severe), and pointwise per VF location
- plot_policy_comparison.py: publication-ready figures (per-k curves,
  severity bars, pointwise heatmaps, compute cost, summary CSV)
- merge_policy_parts.py: merge SLURM array partial outputs into single arrays
- job_pop_order.sh: SLURM job for A6 order computation
- job_policy_array.sh: SLURM array job (4 tasks) for any single policy
- job_metrics.sh: SLURM CPU job for metrics computation
- run_all_policies.sh: master launcher submitting full pipeline

